17592186413731 1080 "2x+5y+z-4=0" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413731 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413731 1083 #uuid "d4795ff7-792e-54da-b148-8c4ee1d289d5" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413718 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413723 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413725 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413728 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413729 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1077 "selection" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413725 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413732 1079 #uuid "261a61c5-5d9c-5e73-a9c8-99e605e6c3e7" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413719 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413721 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413722 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413726 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413727 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1077 "selection" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413721 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413733 1079 #uuid "f3cdc898-7c65-52bc-9785-8f3da0b98b76" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413717 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413720 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413724 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413730 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413731 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1077 "selection" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413717 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413734 1079 #uuid "f6c20a87-b8c2-530d-b3e1-fb8bd507d26c" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413734 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1069 "q-70815" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(0,0,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=2+2t \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}.$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1072 #uuid "34ca6320-0524-59fc-8f68-7b8524566ac6" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413735 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,3⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨2,5,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨2,5,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =-3 \\\\ 2x+5y-z & =-3 \\\\ 2x+5y-z+3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413732 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1069 "q-330499" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-1,3,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨4,0,1⟩.$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1072 #uuid "d60eaae3-858a-5d2f-83b8-ccadfd1429d3" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413736 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-1,3,2⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨4,0,1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =⟨-1,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =-2 \\\\ 4x+z & =-2 \\\\ 4x+z+2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413733 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1069 "q-128410" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,-2,1)$, $P(3,-1,2)$ and $Q(4,2,0).$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1072 #uuid "fc9c30e8-905e-5cc3-9596-440fe740820a" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true] [17592186413737 1074 "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-1,2⟩,$ and $q=⟨4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,2⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨4,2,0⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+5j+5k \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534196 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-2493b28e-9805-515c-9bb7-52400b1ebad9" 17592186413717 "answer-2717e35a-d5d8-5b8d-b82d-51c22326e847" 17592186413718 "answer-4f5bbffd-b662-53da-9146-542052fb7f6e" 17592186413719 "answer-5c7649c7-0f92-5513-b462-907271b682a9" 17592186413720 "answer-88552711-7258-529e-8575-2c6ac297ae0d" 17592186413721 "answer-88a1e7b7-4a66-5740-9c7e-14a39dd3849b" 17592186413722 "answer-9f69fd47-a1f5-5770-8c3d-1d9916854264" 17592186413723 "answer-a11ad414-7674-5c26-950f-59f6a219f5d2" 17592186413724 "answer-a34b8674-3166-5800-b2b6-3d8e2d749e97" 17592186413725 "answer-a3f975fc-9692-533a-ba00-bf7e8438a517" 17592186413726 "answer-b5ddaec5-2f45-5d0e-8c08-e6549f59e357" 17592186413727 "answer-bb1a451c-30a6-598a-a1e4-37120fd4f9f8" 17592186413728 "answer-cf32c54e-7d9c-57e0-ac44-14a3df665bca" 17592186413729 "answer-d3c26dd6-942b-51e3-9221-ce5b6eff63d3" 17592186413730 "answer-d4795ff7-792e-54da-b148-8c4ee1d289d5" 17592186413731 "answer-field-261a61c5-5d9c-5e73-a9c8-99e605e6c3e7" 17592186413732 "answer-field-f3cdc898-7c65-52bc-9785-8f3da0b98b76" 17592186413733 "answer-field-f6c20a87-b8c2-530d-b3e1-fb8bd507d26c" 17592186413734 "question-34ca6320-0524-59fc-8f68-7b8524566ac6" 17592186413735 "question-d6